---
const stats = [
  { num: "26.0k", unit: "", label: "tokens, median, in context before the first reply", lit: 26, of: 64 },
  { num: "70", unit: "%", label: "of all tokens processed went to that starting load", lit: 14, of: 20 },
  { num: "9", unit: "/12", label: "skills listed in every session and never once used", lit: 9, of: 12 },
];
---

<section class="problem" id="problem">
  <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
  <h2>Your agent carries a load <em>before you type a word.</em></h2>
  <p class="section-lede">
    Instruction files, skill lists, MCP servers, memory. The harness sends all of it again on every
    turn, and none of it shows up anywhere you can see. When an agent drifts, you can't tell whether
    it was missing something or buried under it.
  </p>
  <div class="stats">
    {
      stats.map((s) => (
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="num">
            {s.num}
            <small>{s.unit}</small>
          </span>
          <span class="gauge" aria-hidden="true">
            [{Array.from({ length: s.of }, (_, i) => <i class:list={{ on: i < s.lit }} />)}]
          </span>
          <span class="label">{s.label}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="footnote">* Figures from the demo history behind every sample on this page.</p>
</section>
